{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Clutch, backlash, and rotational sources",
  "exampleId": "block-rotational-sources",
  "description": "The clutch closes at 0.5 s and drags its 1 kg·m² load up to the 100 rad/s the speed source reached at 0.1 s, then locks. The backlash leaves the driven inertia standing still until the sine-driven source has taken up half the 0.1 rad gap, at 0.04 s. A torque source of 0.5 N·m drives an inertia with 0.05 N·m·s of damping through a spring-damper, so it settles at 10 rad/s. A constant 0.4 N·m accelerates a shaft load until its load torque steps up at 0.45 s; then it slows down.",
  "duration": 2,
  "revision": 0,
  "blocks": [
